"""E4 adapter for HC-GLAD (Neural Networks 2026; github.com/jindongli-Ai/HC-GLAD @ 4238b20, cloned to ./src).

Same CLI and per-run JSON "part" schema as evalpaper/harness/run_eval.py and the GLADMamba port
(ext/GLADMamba/run_method.py), so collect-style aggregation works on the parts (see ./collect.py).

One run = (HC-GLAD, dataset, fold, hp) with hp in {ubgold, hpfree}:
  * ubgold : the authors' released per-dataset line (src/script/ad_<DS>.sh, parsed with the repo's own
             argparse parser, main.py:arg_parse); datasets without a released line (NCI1, IMDB-BINARY, MUTAG)
             use the modal released configuration over all 12 released ad lines (NOTES.md).
  * hpfree : the repo's argparse defaults (main.py:21-52), except batch_size / batch_size_test which keep the
             per-dataset ubgold value (A1 rule 2 / A14 analogue), plus the a-priori memory-feasibility fallback
             (NOTES.md, "Memory-feasibility rule": NCI1 batch_size_test 16; REDDIT-B hidden_dim 8, num_layers 2).

The method's training and scoring code is used verbatim:
  * src/models, src/layers, src/manifolds, src/optimizers, src/utils/math_utils are imported unchanged (src is put
    first on sys.path, as `python main.py` does);
  * src/utils/data_loader.py: init_structural_encoding / setDuplicate / get_hyperedge_index / get_ad_split_TU /
    get_ad_dataset_TU are extracted with `ast` and executed unchanged (the module-level `from ogb...` import is not
    executed: ogb is unused by these functions and not installed);
  * src/main.py: arg_parse and setup_seed are extracted with `ast`; the per-trial training/evaluation loop
    (main.py:80-185) is copied line by line into fit() below.
Every deviation is marked "# CHANGE" and listed in NOTES.md.

At every evaluation point (epoch % eval_freq == 0) we record test AUROC/AUPRC/FPR95 (UB-GOLD's metric functions;
sklearn roc_auc_score = HC-GLAD's own skm), per-graph test scores in canonical test order (+ the 4 score
components), and the per-graph anomaly scores of the 20% held-out normal training graphs (RandomState(2026 +
1000*fold), identical to the harness): their mean is "holdout_score" (VAL-NORMAL, A3; chunks of batch_size_test);
"holdout_obj" is the training objective on the held-out graphs (chunks of the training batch_size; secondary).

Usage:
  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -B run_method.py --method HC-GLAD --dataset BZR --fold 0 [--hp hpfree]
